## Coordinating through comms

Other agents edit this repository at the same time. `comms` keeps you off their files.
Nothing claims or checks for you here, so do each step yourself, and read the
`using-comms` skill for the details.

1. Pick a name that tells you apart, such as `codex-billing`, and pass `--as <name>` on
   every comms call. `codex`, `agent` and `user` are refused.
2. See who holds what: `comms status --as codex-billing`
3. Claim every file before you change it, shell writes included:
   `comms claim src/auth.ts src/login.ts --as codex-billing --intent "rework the session cookie"`
4. If the claim is refused, do not edit those files another way. Leave a note and take other work:
   `comms note --as codex-billing "@claude-4f9a1c I need src/auth.ts, tell me when it is free"`
5. Before every commit, run `comms check --staged --as codex-billing`.
   If it refuses, run the `git restore --staged` command it prints.
6. When the work is committed, release:
   `comms release --all-mine --as codex-billing --result "committed 4f2a9c1"`

If the working directory gives `operation not permitted`, run from your home folder
and name the repository: `comms --repo /abs/path/to/repo status --as codex-billing`.
